{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Rty86WDkhdKgkvr1WjSgrA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Code lives in `cmd/` (per-utility packages), `pkg/sys/` (syscall wrappers), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), and `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness). Human operators author specs in `docs/`; the orchestrator generates code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`.\n\n**Current State:** Source code exists for `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/cat`, and `cmd/wc` — all complete. No source code exists for `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`, or any rel02.0+ utilities.\n\n**Current Release Priority:** The earliest incomplete release is **rel01.2** (sponge) — spec complete, no implementation on the working branch. Next is rel01.3 (du), then rel02.0 (trivial utilities with pending specs).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n- rel00.0 (testutils, sys, format): source code exists — done. magefiles excluded from generation (DD7).\n- rel01.0 (wc): source code exists — done.\n- rel01.1 (cat): source code exists — done.\n- **rel01.2 (sponge)**: spec complete, no source code — **this is next**.\n- Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks. Per P8, implementation comes first.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/sponge main.go per sponge PRD\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.2-uc001-sponge.yaml (sponge use case -- contains reference to the sponge PRD file)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.2.yaml (sponge test suite with expected behaviors and edge cases)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (reference implementation pattern for argument parsing, SIGPIPE handling, and error formatting)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (reference implementation for parseArgs pattern with long flags and -- terminator)\n      - pkg/sys/signal.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler called by all cmd/ utilities)\n      - go.mod (module path github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils for import statements)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sponge/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"sponge utility -- reads all stdin then writes to output file\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement core sponge behavior per the sponge PRD: read all of stdin into memory, then write the buffered content to the output file specified as the positional command-line argument. If no file argument is given, write buffered stdin to stdout. The two-phase approach (read all, then write) enables safe in-place file modification in pipelines like 'grep pattern file | sponge file'.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement the -a (append) flag per the sponge PRD: when -a is specified, open the output file in append mode instead of truncating. Without -a, create or truncate the output file before writing.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement error handling and exit codes per the sponge PRD: exit 0 on success, exit 1 on any error (stdin read failure, file open/create failure, write failure). Write error messages to stderr in the format 'sponge: <description>'. Install SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at program start.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Parse command-line arguments following the sponge PRD flag specification. Support -a, the -- flag terminator, and any additional flags specified in the PRD. Use manual argument parsing (not the flag package) matching the pattern in cmd/cat/main.go and cmd/wc/main.go.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the cmd/ package structure established by cmd/cat/main.go: package main, const progName, main() calls sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() then parseArgs() then core logic. Import github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys for signal handling.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use manual argument parsing (not the flag standard library package) matching the pattern in cmd/cat/main.go. Support '--' as flag terminator and combined short flags. Handle '-' as a positional argument if the PRD requires it.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The sponge PRD (located in docs/specs/product-requirements/, referenced by the use case) is the authoritative specification. All flag names, error message formats, exit code semantics, and behavioral edge cases must match the PRD exactly. Implement all requirements found in the PRD.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/sponge/main.go exists and compiles successfully with 'go build ./cmd/sponge/' with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"The program reads all of stdin completely before opening or writing to the output file.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"With -a flag, content is appended to the output file. Without -a, the output file is created or truncated before writing.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"When no file argument is provided, buffered stdin is written to stdout.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Error messages are written to stderr prefixed with 'sponge:' and the program exits with code 1 on any error.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60592,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60592},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7892f5f1-f85f-43bb-83ac-2247c0446a64","uuid":"152b3924-09fa-4749-9235-841e99d9a42f"}
